                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \bar \Gamma^\bullet(X)
            a differential cocycle representing a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                its image
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
                in differential forms is the corresponding
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            %li
              %p
                its image
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl(c)
                in non-differential cohomology is the “topological twist” of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge field
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
          %p Other examples:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+algebraic+K-theory"} differential algebraic K-theory
          %h2#differential_stable_cohomology Differential stable cohomology
          %blockquote
            %p the following are ancient notes that need to be brushed up and polished.
          %h3#HopSin Characterization following Hopkins-Singer
          %p
            A standard definition of differential cohomology is in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theory
            with the complex of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            over
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
