                        %mi Γ
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ch: \Gamma^\bullet(-)
                      \\to
                      Z^\bullet(-, \mathbb{R}) \otimes \Gamma^\bullet(*)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
                map.
          %p
            For more details on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+function+complex"} differential function complex
          %h3#characterization_following_bunkeschick Characterization following Bunke-Schick
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following are old notes once taken in a talk by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Strings%2C+Fields%2C+Topology"} Oberwolfach Workshop, June 2009 – Strings, Fields, Topology
          %p
            The following theory of differential cohomology (also called
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong smooth cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"} Ulrich Bunke
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
          %ul
            %li
              %p idea:
              %ul
                %li combine cohomology + differential forms
          %p main diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi R
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi dR
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\hat H(M) &amp;\stackrel{I}{\to}&amp; H^\bullet(M)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{R} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Omega^\bullet_{d=0}(M)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                  H^\bullet_{dR}(M)
                  \\simeq H^\bullet(M,\mathbb{R})
                  }
          %p
            so differential cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H^\bullet(M)
            combines the ordinary cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(M)
            with a differential form representative of its image in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                projects a differential cohomology to its underlying ordinary cohomology class;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                send the differential cohomology class to its
                %em curvature
                differential form data
          %p we want an exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mrow
                              %mo •
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ch
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mo •
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mrow
                            %mi im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi d
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mi d
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi R
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  H^{\bullet-1}(M)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{ch}{\to}&amp;
                  \\Omega^{\bullet-1}(M)/{im(d)}
                  \&amp;\stackrel{d}{\to}&amp;
                  \\hat H(M)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{I}{\to}&amp;
                  H^\bullet(M) \to 0
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  {}_{d}\searrow
                  \&amp;
                  \\downarrow^R
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  \\Omega^\bullet_{d=0}(M)
                  }
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Given cohomology theory
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E^\bullet
              is a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo →
                    %mi Grps
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E : Diff \to Grps
              with transformations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I, R
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi M
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi E
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi M
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi R
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi M
                            %mo ,
                            %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi E
                              %mi dR
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi M
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi E
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi M
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\hat E(M) &amp;\stackrel{I}{\to}&amp; E^\bullet(M)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{R} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{d=0}(M, V)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    E^\bullet_{dR}(M)
                    \\simeq E^\bullet(M,\mathbb{R})
                    }
            %p where
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = E^\bullet(pt)\otimes \mathbb{R}
            %p
              is the graded non-torsion cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              on the point (so now all the gradings above denote total grading)
            %p and such that there is a transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mi im
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a : \Omega^{\bullet -1}(M)/{im(d)}
                    \\to
                    \\hat E^*(M)
            %p that gives the above kind of exact sequence.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
              is multiplicative, we say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E^*
              is multiplicative with product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
              takes values in graded rings and the transformations are compatible with multiplicative structure, where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a(\omega) \vee x = a(\omega \wedge R(x))
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
              has
              = succeed "-integration" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int : \hat E^*(M \times S^1) \to \hat E^{\bullet -1}(M)
            %p
              compatible with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int
              of forms and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              it is given by the suspension isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int \circ p^* = 0
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : M \times S^1 \to M
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi id
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ∫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int \circ (  id \times (z \mapsto \bar z) )^* = - \int
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p Ordinary cohomology theories are supposed to be homotopy invariant, but differential forms are not, so in general the differential cohomology is not.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
              a smooth cohomology theory. The
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong homotopy formula
            %p
              given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi smooth
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : M \times [0,1] \stackrel{smooth}{\to} N
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy"} smooth homotopy
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi h
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi M
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h^*_1(X) - h^*_0(X)
                    \=
                    a( \int_{M \times [0,1]/M}  h^*(R(x)))
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(R)
              (i.e. flat cohomology) is a homotopy invariant functor.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi flat
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H{flat} := ker(R)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_lemma Proof of lemma
            %p It suffices to show
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ι
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ι
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi M
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota_1^*(x) - \iota_0^*(x) = a(\int_{M\times [0,1]/M} R(x))
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \hat E(M \times [0,1])
            %p
              Observe if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = p^* y
              the left hand side vanishes,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int R(p^* y) = 0
            %p
              For general
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} jhat
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists y \in \jhat E(M)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - p^*(y) = a (\omega)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega(M \times [0,1])
            %p
              Stokes’ theorem gives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*_1 \omega - i^*_0 \omega = \int_{[0,1]} d \omega
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} = \int R(a(\omega)) = \int R(x-p^* \omega) = \int R(x)
            %p On the other hand
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i^*_1(x) - i^*_0(x) = i^*_1(a(\omega))
                    \- i^*_0(a(\omega))
                    \= a(\int R(x))
            %p
              A calculation:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mover
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi flat
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H^1_{flat}(pt) = \hat H^1(pt) = \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z} = \hat K^1(pt)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p (Hopkins–Singer)
            %p
              For each generalized cohomology theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
              a differential version
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E^*
              as in the above definition does exist.
            %p
              Moreover
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mover
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi flat
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi E
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E_{flat}^* = E \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}^{\bullet -1}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p It’s not evident how to obtain more structure like multiplication.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Using geometric models, multiplicative smooth extensions with
              = succeed "-integration" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %ul
              %li
                %p K-theory (Bunke–Schick)
              %li
                %p
                  MU-bordisms (unitary bordisms)
                  %br>/
                  (Bunke–Schröder–Schick–Wiethaupts; and from there Landweber exact cohomology theories)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p (Uniqueness theorem due to Bunke–Schick. Simons–Sullivan proved this for ordinary integral cohomology.)
            %p
              Assume
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %em rationally even
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi for
                    %mi odd
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^k(pt)\otimes \mathbb{Q} = 0 \;\; for odd k
            %p plus one further technical assumption.
            %p
              Then any two smooth extensions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E^*
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^*
              are naturally isomorphic.
            %p If required to be compatible with integration the ismorphism is unique.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E, \tilde E
              are multiplicative, then this isomorphism is, as well.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If we don’t require compatibility with
              = succeed "-integration," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat K^1
          %h4#examples_2 Examples
          %h5#differential_cobordism_cohomology_theory Differential cobordism cohomology theory
          %p
            A model for a multiplicative differential refinement of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology+theory"} complex cobordism cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schick"} Thomas Schick
              %em Landweber exact formal group laws and smooth cohomology theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1134"}> arXiv:0711.1134
              )
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cobordism+cohomology+theory"} differential cobordism cohomology theory
