          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Differential cohomology was first developed for the special cases of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            (interest into which came from discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring+theory"} type II superstring theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              %em Differential cohomology in geometry and analysis
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.uni-regensburg.de/Fakultaeten/nat_Fak_I/Bunke/Vortrag-Erlangen.pdf"}> pdf slides
              )
          %p
            The suggestion that differential cohomology is or should be characterized by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#SimonsSullivan07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              %em Axiomatic Characterization of Ordinary Differential Cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701077"}> arXiv:math/0701077
              )
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (discussed there for
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#SimonsSullivan08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
                %em Structured vector bundles define differential K-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4935"}> arXiv:0810.4935
                )
              %p
                (discussed there for
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
          %p
            A first systematic account characterizing and constructing stable differential cohomology in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+products"} homotopy fiber products
            of bare
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            data (which is really the homotopy-theoretic refinement of one of right square in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology,and M-Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0211216"} arXiv:math/0211216
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1143642908"} euclid:1143642908
          %p
            motivated by applications in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization+and+generalized+differential+cohomology"} Dirac charge quantization and generalized differential cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0011220"}> arXiv:hep-th/0011220
              )
          %p with further reviews including
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Valentino"}> Alessandro Valentino
                \:
                %em Differential cohomology and quantum gauge fields
                (2008) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Valentino-DiffCohAndQuantumGauge.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Szabo12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"}> Richard Szabo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantization of Higher Abelian Gauge Theory in Generalized Differential Cohomology
                %em 7th International Conference on Mathematical Methods in Physics (ICMP 2012)
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.2530"}> arXiv:1209.2530
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.22323/1.175.0009"} doi:10.22323/1.175.0009
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1185286"} inspire:1185286
          %p The homotopy-pullback definition of differential generalized cohomology from
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger02"} Hopkins-Singer 02, Section 4.1
          %p is picked up in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
                %em Differential function spectra, the differential Becker-Gottlieb transfer, and applications to differential algebraic K-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1306.0247"}> arXiv:1306.0247
                )
            %li#Bunke12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                , Section 4.3 of:
                %em Differential cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1208.3961"}> arXiv:1208.3961
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"} Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13, Section 4.4
          %p
            The suggestion that differential cohomology is naturally the intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive
            appeared in
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              )
          %p
            and the observation, working with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+spectra"} sheaves of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            canonically sits inside a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              %strong 11
              (2016) 1-66 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5"} doi:10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5
          %p
            Discussion in the generality of differential
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
          %ul
            %li#FSS20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Twisted+Non-Abelian+Cohomology"} The Character Map in Nonabelian Cohomology — Twisted, Differential, Generalizaed
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.11909"} arXiv:2009.11909
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13422"} doi:10.1142/13422
          %p Another book-length overview:
          %ul
            %li#AmabelDebrayHaine21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Araminta+Amabel"}> Araminta Amabel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"} Arun Debray
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+J.+Haine"} Peter J. Haine
              (eds.):
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential Cohomology: Categories, Characteristic Classes, and Connections
              %a{:href => "https://math.mit.edu/juvitop/pastseminars/2019_Fall.html"} Fall 2019 talks at MIT’s Juvitop seminar
              by: A. Amabel, D. Chua, A. Debray, S. Devalapurkar, D. Freed, P. Haine, M. Hopkins, G. Parker, C. Reid, and A. Zhang. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.12250"}> arXiv:2109.12250
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On differential cohomology in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"}> Arun Debray
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential Cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.14338"} arXiv:2312.14338
          %p
            On differential cohomology in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
          %ul
            %li
              Nino Scalbi,
              %em Differential Cohomology as Diffeological Homotopy Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.02593"}> arXiv:2408.02593
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On differential cohomology in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+W.+Moore"}> Gregory W. Moore
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vivek+Saxena"} Vivek Saxena
              = succeed "," do
                %em TASI Lectures On Topological Field Theories And Differential Cohomology
              %a{:href => "https://sites.google.com/colorado.edu/tasi-2023-wiki/home"} TASI 2023
              lecture notes &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07408"}> arXiv:2510.07408
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#lectures_and_talks Lectures and talks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Simons Center Workshop on Differential Cohomology January 10, 2011- January 14, 2011 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.scgp.stonybrook.edu/?q=node/21"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Bunke12"} Bunke 2012
            %li#DG18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Grady"}> Daniel Grady
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential cohomology and Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry, Topology &amp; Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DiffCohomologyAndApplications18.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
